course: dictionary
lesson: 10431
title: The tropics
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The tropics are the hot, wet parts of the Earth near the middle, around the equator. The equator is an imaginary line that circles the Earth halfway between the North Pole and the South Pole. Context helps you find the meaning: «The equator, the Tropic of Cancer, the Tropic of Capricorn and the Arctic Circle are lines of latitude.» Those are lines around the Earth, so a tropic must be a line too.
explain: A tropic is one of two imaginary lines. The Tropic of Cancer is north of the equator and the Tropic of Capricorn is south of it. «Tropic» on its own means one of these lines, while «the tropics» means the whole hot region between them.
explain: The word «tropical» means something that belongs to the tropics. «Tropical rainforest» and «tropical fish» both come from the hot, wet part of the world. «In EU5 the far north has cold, harsh locations and the tropics hot ones, which follows latitude quite well.» Here the context shows that the tropics are the hot places, far from the cold north.
fact: A tropic is one of two imaginary lines around the Earth.
fact: The Tropic of Cancer is about 23.5 degrees north of the equator.
fact: The Tropic of Capricorn is about 23.5 degrees south of the equator.
fact: «The tropics» means the hot, wet region of the Earth near the equator, between the two tropics.
fact: The Tropic of Capricorn passes through Australia, near Rockhampton and Alice Springs.
exercise: What are the tropics? | The deepest parts of the ocean | A kind of bright, sunny cloud | The cold lands near the North Pole | *The hot, wet regions of the Earth near the equator
exercise: «The Tropic of Capricorn passes through Australia.» What is the Tropic of Capricorn? | A river that runs into the sea | A real road across a desert | A mountain in the rainforest | *An imaginary line south of the equator
exercise: «Many great deserts lie near 30 degrees north or south of the equator.» Where do many great deserts lie? | Exactly on the equator | At the North Pole | Under the sea | *Near 30 degrees north or south of the equator
test: «In Britain, north of the Tropic of Cancer, the Sun at midday is due south.» So which way does your midday shadow point in Britain? | South | *North | West | East
test: What does «tropical» mean? | Very tall and thin | Very cold and icy | *Belonging to the tropics, hot and wet near the equator | Lying deep under the sea
exam: Which line lies south of the equator? | *Tropic of Capricorn | Tropic of Cancer | Arctic Circle | Prime meridian at Greenwich
